From: RoboParty <dev@roboparty.com>
Subject: [PATCH] can: gs_usb: opt in to HPM channel bus-off restart

Provide CAN_MODE_START and bus-off notification for the roboto_usb4can
firmware. Keep this experimental path disabled unless the module parameter
hpm_bus_off_restart=1 is explicitly supplied. The firmware must implement
channel-local RESET, purge pending channel traffic, retain timing settings,
echo opaque 32-bit tokens and correctly report START failures.
Match roboto_usb4can v1.1.0 and newer.

Quiesce channel TX before publishing BUS_OFF because CAN core flushes echo
SKBs before calling do_set_mode. Serialize TX and completion paths with the
recovery gate. Restart only the affected channel using RESET, nominal/data
timing and START with the original mode flags; keep shared RX URBs running.

Use per-submission tokens to reject late echoes after restart or an OUT
error. Do not recycle a successful context until both OUT completion and
echo arrive. A token wraps only after roughly 429 million uses of its slot.

Cancel recovery work before closing the channel. Failed USB control
requests leave the channel gated; CAN core does not retry failure.
During restart only, retry START stalls at most five times within a 100 ms
deadline. RESET preserves an in-flight IN buffer until completion, so an
immediate START can temporarily stall. Other errors fail immediately and
closing prevents another attempt. Do not alter first-open or endpoint
ownership handling.
This does not recover USB disconnects or identify stale ordinary
RX/error frames. Hardware bus-off fault injection is not validated.

Signed-off-by: RoboParty <dev@roboparty.com>
